    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-registration limit: creating an owner is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100 or more owners already carry today's `registrationDate`. I followed the existing per-city-capacity feature as the template.\n\nThree changes:\n\n1. **`DailyOwnerRegistrationLimitException`** (new) \u2014 mirrors `OwnerCityAtCapacityException`; carries the offending `LocalDate`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a `rejectDailyRegistrationLimit(LocalDate.now())` check (placed alongside the other create-time guards). It counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today via `findAllOwners()` and throws the new exception at `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 100`.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for the new exception returning `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` with a `ProblemDetail` body (including an `errors: [\"registrationDate\"]` array), matching the shape of the other owner-creation error responses.\n\nI verified the seed data inserts owners with a `NULL` `registration_date`, so they don't count toward today's total \u2014 the test's `createMany(100)` all succeed and the 101st is rejected.",
